## Why This Is Asked
This problem introduces a dynamic programming angle where subarrays are weighted by their block index. It tests the ability to transform interval sums into prefix sums, derive a two-dimensional DP over position and block count, and implement solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) interval sum computation
- 2D DP over position and block count
- Solution reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k); Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScorePartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = [0];
  for (let x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1] + x);
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = P[i];
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
        const score = dp[p][t-1] + (P[i] - P[p]) * t;
        if (score > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = score;
          parent[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct partitions
  const partitions = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = parent[end][t];
    partitions.unshift([start+1, end]);
    end = start;
  }

  return { maxScore: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

Why This Is Asked

Tests DP for non-overlapping intervals with fixed cost and gaps, reflecting scheduling problems.

Key Concepts

- DP with dp[i][t] for first i days and t windows
- Prefix sums for quick window sums
- End-at-i transitions with a preceding gap
- Backpointers for reconstruction
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

Code Example

```javascript
function maxProfitKWindows(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const S = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) S[i] = S[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) {
    for (let t=0;t<=k;t++) {
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if (t>0) {
        for (let s=1;s<=i;s++) {
          if (i- s >= 2) {
            const val = dp[s-2][t-1] + (S[i]-S[s-1]) - c;
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; prv[i][t] = s; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best: dp[n][k], endIndex: n, t: k};
}
```

